---
// Timeline of the errgroup program in the post: fetch id takes id x 100 ms, SetLimit(3), task 2 returns an error.
// Start and end times follow from that arithmetic (not measured), as the caption says.
const x0 = 120;
const k = 2; // px per ms
const rowY = (i: number) => 74 + i * 42;
const bh = 26;
const X = (ms: number) => x0 + ms * k;
const tasks = [
  { id: 1, s: 0, e: 100, kind: 'ok' },
  { id: 2, s: 0, e: 200, kind: 'err' },
  { id: 3, s: 0, e: 200, kind: 'cancel', would: 300 },
  { id: 4, s: 100, e: 200, kind: 'cancel' },
  { id: 5, s: 200, e: 200, kind: 'cancel' },
];
const axisY = rowY(5) - 6;
const W = 900;
const H = axisY + 40;
---
<figure class="gp09eg">
  <div class="gp09eg-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Timeline of five errgroup tasks with a limit of 3. Task 1 finishes at 100 ms. Task 2 fails at 200 ms, which cancels the context. Task 3 and task 4 are cancelled at 200 ms. Task 5 starts at 200 ms with an already cancelled context.">
    <text x="20" y="24" class="gp09eg-h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Five tasks, at most 3 at once</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Năm task, tối đa 3 task cùng lúc</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x={X(200)} y="52" text-anchor="middle" class="gp09eg-muted">
      <tspan data-lang-en>ctx cancelled</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>ctx bị hủy</tspan>
    </text>
    <line x1={X(200)} x2={X(200)} y1="58" y2={axisY} class="gp09eg-cancel" />

    {tasks.map((t, i) => (
      <g>
        <text x="20" y={rowY(i) + 18} class="gp09eg-name">fetch {t.id}</text>
        {t.would && <rect x={X(t.e)} y={rowY(i)} width={(t.would - t.e) * k} height={bh} rx="4" class="gp09eg-would" />}
        {t.e > t.s ? <rect x={X(t.s)} y={rowY(i)} width={(t.e - t.s) * k} height={bh} rx="4" class={t.kind === 'err' ? 'gp09eg-bar is-err' : t.kind === 'ok' ? 'gp09eg-bar is-ok' : 'gp09eg-bar is-cancel'} /> : <line x1={X(t.s)} x2={X(t.s)} y1={rowY(i) - 2} y2={rowY(i) + bh + 2} class="gp09eg-tick" />}
        {t.kind === 'cancel' && t.e > t.s && (
          <text x={X(t.s) + 10} y={rowY(i) + 18} class="gp09eg-onbar">
            <tspan data-lang-en>cancelled</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>bị hủy</tspan>
          </text>
        )}
        {t.kind === 'ok' && (
          <text x={X(t.e) + 8} y={rowY(i) + 18}>
            <tspan data-lang-en>fetch 1 ok</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>fetch 1 ok</tspan>
          </text>
        )}
        {t.kind === 'err' && (
          <text x={X(t.e) + 8} y={rowY(i) + 18} class="gp09eg-bad">
            <tspan data-lang-en>error: upstream returned 503</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>lỗi: upstream returned 503</tspan>
          </text>
        )}
        {t.id === 4 && (
          <text x={X(t.e) + 8} y={rowY(i) + 18}>
            <tspan data-lang-en>starts at 100 ms, in task 1's slot</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>bắt đầu ở 100 ms, vào slot của task 1</tspan>
          </text>
        )}
        {t.id === 5 && (
          <text x={X(t.e) + 8} y={rowY(i) + 18}>
            <tspan data-lang-en>starts at 200 ms, in task 2's slot, leaves at once</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>bắt đầu ở 200 ms, vào slot của task 2, thoát ngay</tspan>
          </text>
        )}
        {t.id === 3 && (
          <text x={X(t.would) + 8} y={rowY(i) + 18} class="gp09eg-muted">
            <tspan data-lang-en>would end at 300 ms</tspan>
            <tspan data-lang-vi>lẽ ra xong ở 300 ms</tspan>
          </text>
        )}
      </g>
    ))}

    <line x1={x0} x2={X(300)} y1={axisY} y2={axisY} class="gp09eg-rule" />
    {[0, 100, 200, 300].map((ms) => (
      <g>
        <line x1={X(ms)} x2={X(ms)} y1={axisY} y2={axisY + 5} class="gp09eg-rule" />
        <text x={X(ms)} y={axisY + 24} text-anchor="middle" class="gp09eg-muted">{ms} ms</text>
      </g>
    ))}
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Task id takes id × 100 ms, so these start and end times follow from the code rather than a measurement. The dashed outline is the time task 3 would still have needed. The failure at 200 ms reaches every task that is waiting on ctx.Done(), including task 5, which never gets to start real work.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Task id mất id × 100 ms, nên các mốc thời gian này suy ra từ code chứ không phải đo. Khung nét đứt là phần thời gian task 3 lẽ ra còn cần. Lỗi ở 200 ms đến mọi task đang chờ ctx.Done(), kể cả task 5, task chưa kịp làm việc thật.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gp09eg { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gp09eg-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gp09eg svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .gp09eg text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .gp09eg .gp09eg-h { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gp09eg .gp09eg-name { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gp09eg .gp09eg-bad { fill: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }
  .gp09eg .gp09eg-muted { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp09eg-rule { stroke: var(--border); }
  .gp09eg figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
  .gp09eg-bar.is-ok { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp09eg-bar.is-cancel { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gp09eg-bar.is-err { fill: var(--red); }
  .gp09eg .gp09eg-onbar { fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp09eg-would { fill: none; stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; }
  .gp09eg-tick { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 2; }
  .gp09eg-cancel { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
</style>
